WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.809
A sheet CRM is enough.

00:00:01.809 --> 00:00:03.257
Fancy tools can wait.

00:00:03.257 --> 00:00:05.428
This lesson is about sheet crm.

00:00:05.428 --> 00:00:08.322
Name / source / next step / status.

00:00:08.322 --> 00:00:10.855
Do not treat this as theory only.

00:00:10.855 --> 00:00:14.474
Treat it as a move you can run this week.

00:00:14.474 --> 00:00:19.902
By the end, you should be able to act without waiting for a perfect plan.

00:00:19.902 --> 00:00:23.882
Keep the DigProg habit: watch, practice, then take one real action.

00:00:23.882 --> 00:00:28.224
Stay practical: build a 20-row CRM before you optimize branding or tools.

00:00:28.544 --> 00:00:30.904
Columns: name, source, next step, status.

00:00:30.904 --> 00:00:32.478
That is the spine.

00:00:32.478 --> 00:00:35.232
Remember the objective: build a 20-row CRM.

00:00:35.232 --> 00:00:39.559
Write the idea in your own words before you move on.

00:00:39.559 --> 00:00:44.280
Name one concrete next action you can finish in under an hour.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:48.608
Avoid vanity work that feels busy but does not create proof.

00:00:48.608 --> 00:00:53.329
If something is unclear, simplify the promise and try a smaller version.

00:00:53.329 --> 00:00:56.082
Talk to a real person when possible.

00:00:56.082 --> 00:00:57.656
Feedback beats guessing alone.

